1
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:04,815
Water...

2
00:00:05,358 --> 00:00:07,025
Earth...

3
00:00:07,652 --> 00:00:09,611
Fire...

4
00:00:09,904 --> 00:00:12,114
Air.

5
00:00:13,157 --> 00:00:16,576
My grandmother used to
tell me stories about the old days.

6
00:00:16,661 --> 00:00:18,245
A time of peace,

7
00:00:18,329 --> 00:00:20,998
when the Avatar kept balance
between Water Tribes,

8
00:00:21,082 --> 00:00:22,791
Earth Kingdom, Fire Nation,

9
00:00:22,875 --> 00:00:24,501
and Air Nomads.

10
00:00:24,585 --> 00:00:27,504
But that all changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

11
00:00:31,467 --> 00:00:35,012
Only the Avatar
mastered all four elements.

12
00:00:35,096 --> 00:00:38,557
Only he could stop
the ruthless firebenders.

13
00:00:38,641 --> 00:00:41,435
But when the world needed him most,
he vanished.

14
00:00:44,355 --> 00:00:46,064
A hundred years have passed,

15
00:00:46,149 --> 00:00:48,942
and the Fire Nation
is nearing victory in the war.

16
00:00:50,111 --> 00:00:52,446
Two years ago, my father
and the men of my tribe

17
00:00:52,530 --> 00:00:55,949
journeyed to the Earth Kingdom
to help fight against the Fire Nation,

18
00:00:56,034 --> 00:00:58,827
leaving me and my brother
to look after our tribe.

19
00:00:59,996 --> 00:01:03,874
Some people believe that the Avatar
Was never reborn into the Air Nomads,

20
00:01:03,958 --> 00:01:05,584
and that the cycle is broken.

21
00:01:06,002 --> 00:01:07,627
But I haven't lost hope.

22
00:01:08,004 --> 00:01:09,629
I still believe that somehow

23
00:01:09,714 --> 00:01:12,883
the Avatar will return to save the world.

24
00:01:58,096 --> 00:02:00,055
It's not getting away from me this time.

25
00:02:00,348 --> 00:02:01,515
Watch and learn, Katara.

26
00:02:01,891 --> 00:02:03,350
This is how you catch a fish.

27
00:02:13,945 --> 00:02:15,320
Sokka, look!

28
00:02:15,613 --> 00:02:17,239
Shh, Katara.

29
00:02:17,323 --> 00:02:19,324
You're gonna scare him away.

30
00:02:19,409 --> 00:02:21,326
I can already smell it cooking.

31
00:02:21,911 --> 00:02:24,246
But, Sokka, I caught one.

32
00:02:26,207 --> 00:02:27,374
Hey!

33
00:02:27,458 --> 00:02:28,708
Aah!

34
00:02:29,127 --> 00:02:30,794
Why is it that every time

35
00:02:30,878 --> 00:02:32,504
you play with magic water,

36
00:02:32,588 --> 00:02:33,964
I get soaked?

37
00:02:35,133 --> 00:02:37,634
It's not magic. It's waterbending.

38
00:02:37,718 --> 00:02:38,802
And it's--

39
00:02:38,886 --> 00:02:41,263
Yeah, yeah. An ancient art
unique to our culture,

40
00:02:41,347 --> 00:02:42,347
Blah, blah, blah...

41
00:02:42,432 --> 00:02:44,766
Look, I'm just saying that
if I had weird powers,

42
00:02:44,851 --> 00:02:46,393
I'd keep my weirdness to myself.

43
00:02:46,477 --> 00:02:48,270
You're calling me weird?

44
00:02:48,438 --> 00:02:50,647
I'm not the one
who makes muscles at myself

45
00:02:50,731 --> 00:02:53,358
every time I see my reflection
in the water.

46
00:03:09,208 --> 00:03:10,500
Watch out!

47
00:03:11,586 --> 00:03:12,669
-Aah!
-Go left!

48
00:03:12,753 --> 00:03:13,837
Go left!

49
00:03:17,425 --> 00:03:20,927
Aah!

50
00:03:25,808 --> 00:03:27,058
You call that left?

51
00:03:27,143 --> 00:03:28,560
You don't like my steering.

52
00:03:28,644 --> 00:03:31,813
Well, maybe you should have
waterbended us out of the ice.

53
00:03:31,981 --> 00:03:34,649
-So it's my fault.
-I knew I should have left you home.

54
00:03:35,109 --> 00:03:36,985
Leave it to a girl to screw things up.

55
00:03:39,238 --> 00:03:43,450
You are the most sexist, immature,
nutbrained--

56
00:03:43,701 --> 00:03:46,161
I'm embarrassed to be related to you!

57
00:03:48,956 --> 00:03:51,917
Ever since mom died, I've been doing
all the work around camp,

58
00:03:52,001 --> 00:03:53,835
while you've been off playing soldier.

59
00:03:54,045 --> 00:03:55,545
Katara...

60
00:03:55,630 --> 00:03:57,589
I even wash all the clothes!

61
00:03:57,673 --> 00:04:00,383
Have you ever smelled your dirty socks?

62
00:04:00,510 --> 00:04:01,635
Let me tell you.

63
00:04:01,719 --> 00:04:03,011
Not pleasant!

64
00:04:03,346 --> 00:04:05,138
Katara! Settle down!

65
00:04:05,223 --> 00:04:08,058
No! That's it. I'm done helping you.

66
00:04:08,267 --> 00:04:10,644
From now on, you're on your own!

67
00:04:24,450 --> 00:04:27,410
Okay. You've gone from weird
to freakish, Katara.

68
00:04:27,495 --> 00:04:29,204
You mean, I did that?

69
00:04:29,288 --> 00:04:31,831
Yep. Congratulations.

70
00:05:03,739 --> 00:05:06,491
He's alive. We have to help.

71
00:05:06,576 --> 00:05:08,618
Katara! Get back here!

72
00:05:08,911 --> 00:05:10,537
We don't know what that thing is.

73
00:05:44,363 --> 00:05:45,739
Finally.

74
00:05:45,948 --> 00:05:48,366
Uncle, do you realize what this means?

75
00:05:48,743 --> 00:05:50,869
I won't get to finish my game?

76
00:05:51,078 --> 00:05:53,663
It means my search
is about to come to an end.

77
00:05:56,834 --> 00:05:59,586
That light came from
an incredibly powerful source.

78
00:05:59,670 --> 00:06:00,920
It has to be him.

79
00:06:01,255 --> 00:06:04,049
Or it's just the celestial lights.

80
00:06:04,258 --> 00:06:06,968
We've been down this road before,
Prince Zuko.

81
00:06:07,178 --> 00:06:10,597
I don't want you
to get too excited over nothing.

82
00:06:11,766 --> 00:06:13,350
Please, sit.

83
00:06:13,559 --> 00:06:18,021
Why don't you enjoy
a cup of calming jasmine tea?

84
00:06:18,356 --> 00:06:20,190
I don't need any calming tea!

85
00:06:20,274 --> 00:06:22,067
I need to capture the Avatar!

86
00:06:22,276 --> 00:06:24,861
Helmsman, head a course for the light.

87
00:06:44,382 --> 00:06:45,548
Stop!

88
00:07:01,982 --> 00:07:03,108
Stop it!

89
00:07:14,954 --> 00:07:17,288
I need to ask you something.

90
00:07:17,373 --> 00:07:18,540
What?

91
00:07:18,708 --> 00:07:20,834
Please, come closer.

92
00:07:21,001 --> 00:07:22,210
What is it?

93
00:07:23,546 --> 00:07:25,338
Will you go penguin-sailing with me?

94
00:07:25,798 --> 00:07:27,632
Sure.

95
00:07:27,925 --> 00:07:29,092
I guess.

96
00:07:30,344 --> 00:07:32,178
What's going on here?

97
00:07:32,263 --> 00:07:33,388
You tell us!

98
00:07:33,472 --> 00:07:35,056
How did you get in the ice?

99
00:07:35,141 --> 00:07:36,433
And why aren't you frozen?

100
00:07:36,851 --> 00:07:37,892
I'm not sure.

101
00:07:45,401 --> 00:07:47,652
Appa, are you all right?

102
00:07:48,070 --> 00:07:50,488
Wake up, buddy.

103
00:07:59,540 --> 00:08:02,417
Ha ha! You're okay.

104
00:08:08,174 --> 00:08:09,549
What is that thing?

105
00:08:09,675 --> 00:08:11,217
This is Appa, my flying bison.

106
00:08:11,302 --> 00:08:14,262
Right. And this is Katara,
my flying sister.

107
00:08:18,184 --> 00:08:20,643
Look out!

108
00:08:26,734 --> 00:08:28,151
Don't worry. It'll wash out.

109
00:08:30,863 --> 00:08:32,530
So, do you guys live around here?

110
00:08:32,907 --> 00:08:35,533
Don't answer that.
Did you see that crazy bolt of light?

111
00:08:35,618 --> 00:08:37,869
He was probably trying
to signal the Fire Navy.

112
00:08:37,953 --> 00:08:40,246
Yeah.
I'm sure he's a spy for the Fire Navy.

113
00:08:40,331 --> 00:08:43,249
You can tell by that evil look in his eye.

114
00:08:45,169 --> 00:08:47,378
The paranoid one is my brother Sokka.

115
00:08:47,630 --> 00:08:49,130
You never told us your name.

116
00:08:49,632 --> 00:08:51,466
I'm-- Ah! Ah!

117
00:08:54,845 --> 00:08:57,263
Ah-choo!

118
00:09:04,063 --> 00:09:06,064
I'm Aang.

119
00:09:07,107 --> 00:09:10,318
You just sneezed
and flew ten feet in the air.

120
00:09:10,402 --> 00:09:11,986
Really? It felt higher than that.

121
00:09:12,571 --> 00:09:14,197
You're an airbender.

122
00:09:14,490 --> 00:09:15,657
Sure am.

123
00:09:15,741 --> 00:09:18,326
Giant light beams,
flying bison, airbenders--

124
00:09:18,410 --> 00:09:20,245
I think I got midnight sun madness.

125
00:09:20,538 --> 00:09:22,539
I'm going home to where stuff makes sense.

126
00:09:26,877 --> 00:09:30,129
Well, if you guys are stuck,
Appa and I can give you a lift.

127
00:09:33,425 --> 00:09:35,009
We'd love a ride, thanks.

128
00:09:35,261 --> 00:09:38,638
No! I am not getting
on that fluffy snot monster.

129
00:09:38,764 --> 00:09:41,641
Are you hoping some other
kind of monster will come along

130
00:09:41,725 --> 00:09:43,017
and give you a ride home?

131
00:09:43,310 --> 00:09:45,562
You know, before you freeze to death.

132
00:09:50,901 --> 00:09:53,486
Okay! First-time flyers, hold on tight.

133
00:09:53,863 --> 00:09:55,905
Appa, yip yip!

134
00:10:04,999 --> 00:10:06,749
Come on, Appa, yip yip.

135
00:10:07,626 --> 00:10:10,128
Wow, that was truly amazing.

136
00:10:10,379 --> 00:10:11,504
Appa's just tired.

137
00:10:11,589 --> 00:10:14,716
A little rest and he'll
be soaring through the sky. You'll see.

138
00:10:18,554 --> 00:10:20,346
Why are you smiling at me like that?

139
00:10:20,639 --> 00:10:22,390
I was smiling?

140
00:10:38,866 --> 00:10:40,617
I'm going to bed now.

141
00:10:43,412 --> 00:10:46,581
Yep. A man needs his rest.

142
00:10:47,750 --> 00:10:51,502
Prince Zuko, you need some sleep.

143
00:10:51,921 --> 00:10:53,796
Even if you're right,

144
00:10:53,881 --> 00:10:57,634
and the Avatar is alive,
you won't find him.

145
00:10:58,427 --> 00:11:04,307
Your father, grandfather, and
great-grandfather all tried and failed.

146
00:11:04,725 --> 00:11:08,186
Because their honor
didn't hinge on the Avatar's capture.

147
00:11:08,270 --> 00:11:09,812
Mine does.

148
00:11:09,897 --> 00:11:12,148
This coward's hundred years
in hiding are over.

149
00:11:23,744 --> 00:11:24,744
Hey.

150
00:11:25,496 --> 00:11:27,413
Hey. What are you thinking about?

151
00:11:27,665 --> 00:11:29,248
I guess I was wondering.

152
00:11:29,333 --> 00:11:31,167
Your being an airbender and all...

153
00:11:31,377 --> 00:11:33,670
If you had any idea
what happened to the Avatar.

154
00:11:34,421 --> 00:11:37,465
No. I didn't know him.

155
00:11:37,549 --> 00:11:39,717
I mean, I knew people that knew him.

156
00:11:39,802 --> 00:11:41,844
But I didn't. Sorry.

157
00:11:41,929 --> 00:11:43,471
Okay. Just curious.

158
00:11:43,847 --> 00:11:46,432
-Good night.
-Sleep tight.

159
00:12:31,103 --> 00:12:33,104
Aang. Aang, wake up!

160
00:12:34,314 --> 00:12:36,733
It's okay. We're in the village now.

161
00:12:36,984 --> 00:12:38,151
Come on, get ready.

162
00:12:38,235 --> 00:12:39,736
Everyone's waiting to meet you.

163
00:12:54,501 --> 00:12:57,503
Aang, this is the entire village.

164
00:12:58,005 --> 00:13:00,590
Entire village, Aang.

165
00:13:03,177 --> 00:13:06,596
Why are they all
looking at me like that?

166
00:13:07,139 --> 00:13:08,514
Did Appa sneeze on me?

167
00:13:08,766 --> 00:13:11,726
Well, no one has seen an airbender
in a hundred years.

168
00:13:11,935 --> 00:13:13,352
We thought they were extinct.

169
00:13:13,896 --> 00:13:16,147
Until my granddaughter
and grandson found you.

170
00:13:16,732 --> 00:13:18,232
Extinct?

171
00:13:18,317 --> 00:13:19,776
Aang, this is my grandmother.

172
00:13:20,152 --> 00:13:21,694
Call me Gran Gran.

173
00:13:22,863 --> 00:13:24,655
What is this, a weapon?

174
00:13:24,865 --> 00:13:26,532
You can't stab anything with this.

175
00:13:26,742 --> 00:13:29,786
It's not for stabbing.
It's for airbending.

176
00:13:31,413 --> 00:13:33,206
Magic trick, do it again!

177
00:13:33,707 --> 00:13:35,541
Not magic, airbending.

178
00:13:35,876 --> 00:13:39,045
It lets me control the air currents
around my glider and fly.

179
00:13:39,421 --> 00:13:41,172
You know, last time I checked,

180
00:13:41,256 --> 00:13:42,924
humans can't fly.

181
00:13:43,217 --> 00:13:44,759
Check again!

182
00:13:47,513 --> 00:13:49,347
Wow, he's flying.

183
00:13:53,018 --> 00:13:54,435
He's amazing!

184
00:13:59,775 --> 00:14:01,109
Unh!

185
00:14:06,448 --> 00:14:08,491
My watchtower.

186
00:14:12,121 --> 00:14:13,538
That was amazing.

187
00:14:18,961 --> 00:14:20,336
Great.

188
00:14:20,462 --> 00:14:22,630
You're an airbender,
Katara's a waterbender.

189
00:14:22,714 --> 00:14:25,091
Together you can just
waste time all day long.

190
00:14:25,551 --> 00:14:26,759
You're a waterbender!

191
00:14:27,010 --> 00:14:29,137
Well, sort of. Not yet.

192
00:14:29,471 --> 00:14:30,888
All right. No more playing.

193
00:14:31,473 --> 00:14:33,808
Come on, Katara. You have chores.

194
00:14:34,184 --> 00:14:36,686
I told you.
He's the real thing, Gran Gran.

195
00:14:36,854 --> 00:14:38,855
I finally found a bender to teach me.

196
00:14:39,273 --> 00:14:42,525
Katara, try not to put
all your hopes in this boy.

197
00:14:42,609 --> 00:14:44,652
But he's special. I can tell.

198
00:14:45,112 --> 00:14:48,156
I sense he's filled with much wisdom.

199
00:14:48,824 --> 00:14:52,076
See? Now my wand is stuck to my tongue.

200
00:14:59,001 --> 00:15:00,418
Again.

201
00:15:00,878 --> 00:15:03,254
Hiya!

202
00:15:04,548 --> 00:15:06,757
No!

203
00:15:06,842 --> 00:15:09,844
Power and firebending
come from the breath,

204
00:15:09,970 --> 00:15:11,971
not the muscles.

205
00:15:12,973 --> 00:15:16,184
The breath becomes energy in the body.

206
00:15:16,435 --> 00:15:20,855
The energy extends past your limbs
and becomes fire!

207
00:15:20,939 --> 00:15:22,940
Get it right this time.

208
00:15:23,275 --> 00:15:26,485
Enough. I've been drilling
this sequence all day.

209
00:15:26,570 --> 00:15:28,779
Teach me the next set.
I'm more than ready.

210
00:15:28,864 --> 00:15:30,406
No! You're impatient.

211
00:15:31,200 --> 00:15:33,492
You have yet to master your basics.

212
00:15:33,660 --> 00:15:34,994
Drill it again!

213
00:15:35,329 --> 00:15:36,579
Hiya!

214
00:15:39,082 --> 00:15:43,044
The sages tell us that the Avatar
is the last airbender.

215
00:15:43,128 --> 00:15:45,838
He must be over
a hundred years old by now.

216
00:15:45,923 --> 00:15:48,216
He's had a century
to master the four elements.

217
00:15:48,300 --> 00:15:51,510
I'll need more
than basic firebending to defeat him.

218
00:15:51,595 --> 00:15:54,138
You will teach me the advanced set!

219
00:15:55,682 --> 00:16:00,686
Very well. But first,
I must finish my roast duck.

220
00:16:01,647 --> 00:16:02,939
Yum, yum, yum.

221
00:16:05,067 --> 00:16:07,902
Now, men, it's important
that you show no fear

222
00:16:07,986 --> 00:16:09,487
when you face a firebender.

223
00:16:09,571 --> 00:16:12,990
In the Water Tribe,
we fight till the last man's standing.

224
00:16:13,075 --> 00:16:16,077
For without courage,
how can we call ourselves men?

225
00:16:19,039 --> 00:16:20,373
I gotta pee.

226
00:16:20,666 --> 00:16:23,334
Listen! Until your fathers
return from the war,

227
00:16:23,418 --> 00:16:26,045
they're counting on you
to be the men of this tribe.

228
00:16:26,129 --> 00:16:28,172
And that means no potty breaks.

229
00:16:28,340 --> 00:16:29,590
But I really gotta go.

230
00:16:31,134 --> 00:16:33,302
Okay. Who else has to go?

231
00:16:37,182 --> 00:16:39,225
Have you seen Aang?

232
00:16:39,309 --> 00:16:41,602
Gran Gran said
he disappeared over an hour ago.

233
00:16:42,229 --> 00:16:44,939
Wow! Everything freezes in there.

234
00:16:46,692 --> 00:16:48,401
Katara, get him out of here.

235
00:16:48,485 --> 00:16:50,861
This lesson is for warriors only.

236
00:16:50,946 --> 00:16:51,946
Wee!

237
00:16:52,030 --> 00:16:53,906
Ha! Ha! Ha!

238
00:16:57,035 --> 00:16:58,911
Stop! Stop it right now!

239
00:16:59,663 --> 00:17:00,997
What's wrong with you?

240
00:17:01,081 --> 00:17:03,749
We don't have time for fun and games
with a war going on!

241
00:17:03,875 --> 00:17:05,251
What war?

242
00:17:05,335 --> 00:17:06,711
What are you talking about?

243
00:17:06,962 --> 00:17:08,045
You're kidding, right?

244
00:17:09,006 --> 00:17:10,923
Penguin!

245
00:17:17,055 --> 00:17:19,223
He's kidding, right?

246
00:17:25,605 --> 00:17:27,440
Aang!

247
00:17:28,150 --> 00:17:30,318
Ha! Ha! Hey, come on, little guy.

248
00:17:30,402 --> 00:17:32,486
Wanna go sledding? Unh!

249
00:17:34,781 --> 00:17:36,407
I have a way with animals.

250
00:17:41,830 --> 00:17:45,374
Aang, I'll help you catch a penguin,
if you teach me waterbending.

251
00:17:46,084 --> 00:17:48,002
You got a deal.

252
00:17:48,253 --> 00:17:49,837
Just one little problem.

253
00:17:50,047 --> 00:17:51,839
I'm an airbender, not a waterbender.

254
00:17:51,923 --> 00:17:54,467
Isn't there someone
in your tribe who can teach you?

255
00:17:55,218 --> 00:17:59,513
No. You're looking at the only waterbender
in the whole South Pole.

256
00:17:59,681 --> 00:18:01,140
This isn't right.

257
00:18:01,224 --> 00:18:02,975
A waterbender needs to master water.

258
00:18:04,186 --> 00:18:05,978
What about the North Pole?

259
00:18:06,063 --> 00:18:08,272
There's another water tribe
up there, right?

260
00:18:08,398 --> 00:18:10,733
Maybe they have waterbenders
who could teach you.

261
00:18:10,817 --> 00:18:12,610
Maybe, but we haven't had contact

262
00:18:12,694 --> 00:18:15,196
with our sister tribe in a long time.

263
00:18:15,364 --> 00:18:18,199
It's not exactly turn right
at the second glacier.

264
00:18:18,283 --> 00:18:20,034
It's on the other side of the world.

265
00:18:20,160 --> 00:18:22,536
But you forget. I have a flying bison.

266
00:18:22,621 --> 00:18:26,123
Appa and I can personally
fly you to the North Pole.

267
00:18:26,208 --> 00:18:28,250
Katara, we're gonna find you a master.

268
00:18:28,460 --> 00:18:30,669
That's... I mean...

269
00:18:30,754 --> 00:18:33,589
I don't know. I've never left home before.

270
00:18:33,673 --> 00:18:35,007
Well, you think about it.

271
00:18:35,092 --> 00:18:38,469
But in the meantime, can you teach me
to catch one of these penguins?

272
00:18:39,346 --> 00:18:42,723
Okay. Listen closely, my young pupil.

273
00:18:42,808 --> 00:18:45,851
Catching penguins
is an ancient and sacred art.

274
00:18:46,353 --> 00:18:48,145
Observe.

275
00:18:51,566 --> 00:18:54,568
Ha! Ha! Ha! Ha!

276
00:19:03,662 --> 00:19:06,539
Ha! Ha! Yeah!

277
00:19:10,460 --> 00:19:11,710
Whoo!

278
00:19:15,715 --> 00:19:18,884
-I haven't done this since I was a kid.
-You still are a kid!

279
00:19:40,824 --> 00:19:42,199
Whoa...

280
00:19:42,826 --> 00:19:44,660
What is that?

281
00:19:44,870 --> 00:19:46,537
A Fire Navy ship,

282
00:19:46,913 --> 00:19:49,248
and a very bad memory for my people.

283
00:19:52,544 --> 00:19:53,919
Aang, stop.

284
00:19:54,004 --> 00:19:55,546
We're not allowed to go near it.

285
00:19:55,630 --> 00:19:57,256
The ship could be booby-trapped.

286
00:19:57,382 --> 00:20:00,009
If you want to be a bender,
you have to let go of fear.

287
00:20:47,140 --> 00:20:50,684
This ship has haunted my tribe
since Gran Gran was a little girl.

288
00:20:50,977 --> 00:20:53,354
It was part of
the Fire Nation's first attacks.

289
00:20:54,314 --> 00:20:55,981
Okay. Back up.

290
00:20:56,274 --> 00:20:57,942
I have friends all over the world,

291
00:20:58,026 --> 00:20:59,318
even in the Fire Nation.

292
00:20:59,402 --> 00:21:00,819
I've never seen any war.

293
00:21:00,946 --> 00:21:03,364
Aang, how long were you in that iceberg?

294
00:21:03,907 --> 00:21:06,492
I don't know. A few days maybe...

295
00:21:06,701 --> 00:21:09,495
I think it was more like a hundred years.

296
00:21:10,080 --> 00:21:11,664
What? That's impossible.

297
00:21:12,123 --> 00:21:14,333
Do I look like a 112-year-old man to you?

298
00:21:14,584 --> 00:21:15,626
Think about it.

299
00:21:15,710 --> 00:21:17,419
The war is a century old.

300
00:21:17,546 --> 00:21:20,589
You don't know about it, because somehow

301
00:21:20,674 --> 00:21:22,883
you were in there that whole time.

302
00:21:23,134 --> 00:21:24,969
It's the only explanation.

303
00:21:26,763 --> 00:21:28,681
A hundred years.

304
00:21:29,015 --> 00:21:30,724
I can't believe it.

305
00:21:30,809 --> 00:21:32,601
I'm sorry, Aang.

306
00:21:32,686 --> 00:21:35,563
Maybe, somehow,
there's a bright side to all this.

307
00:21:35,897 --> 00:21:37,273
I did get to meet you.

308
00:21:38,984 --> 00:21:40,818
Come on. Let's get out of here.

309
00:21:47,534 --> 00:21:50,286
Aang, let's head back.
This place is creepy.

310
00:21:54,291 --> 00:21:56,625
What's that you said about booby traps?

311
00:22:10,765 --> 00:22:12,016
Hold on tight!

312
00:22:23,570 --> 00:22:25,654
The last airbender.

313
00:22:26,323 --> 00:22:28,115
Quite agile for his old age.

314
00:22:29,117 --> 00:22:33,412
Wake my uncle!
Tell him I found the Avatar.

315
00:22:39,377 --> 00:22:41,295
As well as his hiding place.
